          "turn_index": 2,
          "type": "turn",
          "question": "When would they actually be needed?",
          "answer": "The guidance I could retrieve does not say when antibiotics are needed for a cold or the cough after it. The passage from \"Upper respiratory infection: antibiotic stewardship and when antibiotics are indicated\" describes the default position of not prescribing them for these infections, but the text I received stops before it lists any exceptions. I can't fill that gap from memory.\n\nThe influenza guidance says antibiotics are reserved for bacterial complications, such as a secondary bacterial infection. That is a general point from a different illness, so it doesn't tell us what applies to you.\n\nA clinician can examine you and decide whether a bacterial infection is likely. This is the same reason for the warning signs I listed earlier: a cough that gets worse, a return of illness after you had started to recover, shortness of breath, chest pain, or a high fever.\n\nSources: Upper respiratory infection: antibiotic stewardship and when antibiotics are indicated; Influenza: annual vaccination and the timing of antiviral treatment.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
